diff --git a/docs/METHODOLOGY_GUIDE.md b/docs/METHODOLOGY_GUIDE.md
index 1418d1c..3970579 100644
--- a/docs/METHODOLOGY_GUIDE.md
+++ b/docs/METHODOLOGY_GUIDE.md
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ For example, one person on {{value:example.gross}} a year in {{value:example.cit
 
 Every amount is for a full year (the drawer can also show it per month), in US dollars, so jobs in different countries sit on the same scale.
 
-- **Gross pay** is the middle of the job's posted base-pay range. Pay quoted by the hour or the month is turned into a yearly figure first, then converted to US dollars. When one posting gives a range for each of several places, each place is scored on its own range (the drawer lists them under **Pay by place**); when it gives a range for each of several levels, the middle is taken across all of them, from the lowest to the highest (listed under **Pay by level**). A posted minimum ("from €46K") counts as that minimum, and an hourly rate that the posting says includes the highest shift differential counts as posted. Part-time hourly pay is counted on the hours a week the posting states; with no hours stated there is no score. Pay for an internship or another fixed-term programme counts for that term only when the posting says how long it lasts, so the drawer shows it per month and for the whole term; with no length stated, it is turned into a yearly figure like a salary. Pay posted for one country is never used for an office in another country.
